per Warbler which can frequent the same reed beds, but the latter is colder brown, does not have the grey tint in the front of the body, has a stronger beak and shows very long undertail feathers. Similar species Savi's Warbler Chestnut-headed Tesia Chestnut-crowned Bush Warbler Distribution ♂ adulte plum. internuptial sp. Cettia cetti ♂ adulte sp. Cettia cetti Cetti's Warbler occupies a variable width band that stretches from the Atlantic to central Asia and eastern Kazakhstan. To the west, it is mainly Mediterranean, occupying the coast of the Mediterranean, except for Libya and Egypt, but it also moves north on the Atlantic coast due to the oceanic climate. This is why it can be found everywhere in France, except for the extreme northeast, and occasionally in the south-east of the UK. It is sedentary there. On the other hand, the populations of the extreme south of western Russia, Kazakhstan and inner Turkey are migratory and winter in the southern part of the nesting area, but also disjointly up to the Persian Gulf and the north of the Indian Ocean. Additional data Migration Full Migrant | Sedentary Bird et al. 2020, Tobias et al. 2021 Domaine biogéographique Palearctic Pigot et al. 2020 Aire 5290133.33 km² Bird et al. 2020, Tobias et al. 2021 Latitudes de reproduction 27,2 à 54,7 ° Tobias et al. 2021 Aire restreinte N Birdlife's Worldbird Database Voice song and calls ▶ 0:00 / 0:00 ▶ Song 0:18 Vatéra, Lesbos, North Aegean (Greece) Didier Collin CC BY-NC ▶ Call, song 0:25 Saint-Vigor-d'Ymonville, Seine-Maritime, Normandie (France) Olivier Swift CC BY-NC-SA ▶ Alarm call 0:19 Saintes-Maries-de-la-Mer, Bouches-du-Rhone, Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur (France) Fernand Deroussen CC BY-NC-ND ▶ Song 0:02 Petit-Mars, Loire-Atlantique, Pays de la Loire (France) Manuel Grosselet CC BY-NC-SA ▶ Song 0:04 Sablons, Isère, Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes (France) Vincent Palomares CC BY-NC-SA ▶ Song 0:07 Oued Seguen, Teleghma, Wilaya de Mila (Algeria) Karim Haddad CC BY-NC-SA ▶ Song 0:11 Sai